Configure multicast DNS

If you're using DHCP, your IP address may change from time to time. On your Helios machine you can enable Multicast DNS:

```
# svcadm enable network/dns/multicast
```

You should then be able to find the machine from your workstation as myhostname.local, rather than needing to use the IP address.